   "cell_type": "raw",
   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"# Home Task (Experiment 5): Naive Bayes Classification\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"**Objective**\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- Train a **Naive Bayes** classifier on a suitable dataset.\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- Practice the standard ML workflow: **load → inspect → clean → split → train → evaluate**.\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"**Note on features**\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- `GaussianNB` expects **numeric** features.\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- If your dataset contains **categorical (string)** columns, encode them first (e.g., One-Hot Encoding).\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f1c6c8f1\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"import pandas as pd\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b9f64a2e\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 1) Load dataset\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"We load the CSV file into a pandas DataFrame.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c8a06b8d\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df = pd.read_csv('Naive-Bayes-Classification-Data.csv')\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d364d1a0\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 2) Quick inspection\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"Show the dataframe and check its dimensions.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"a5d9e98c\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1f8d0d3b\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df.shape\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"aa66c06e\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 3) Data cleaning: duplicates\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"Remove duplicate rows (if any) to avoid biased training/evaluation.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d67163cc\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df.duplicated().sum()\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d88f1d26\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df = df.drop_duplicates()\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"52b57b35\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df.shape\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"45ff41e8\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 4) Missing values\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"Check for nulls before modeling.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"5c8460d1\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"df.isnull().sum()\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"06bcb7bb\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 5) Split into features (X) and target (y)\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- **X**: all columns except the last\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- **y**: the last column (class label)\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1c5b1da7\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"X = df.iloc[:, :-1]\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"y = df.iloc[:, -1]\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9b3ad45b\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"Inspect class distribution (helps detect imbalance).\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9b0e8f16\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"y.value_counts()\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"0ee6f1a3\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 6) Convert features to numeric array\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"This notebook uses `X.values` directly. This is fine **only if** all feature columns are already numeric.\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"If you have categorical columns, replace this step with an encoder (e.g., `OneHotEncoder`).\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"0fb00c78\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"X_encoded = X.values\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f9a25116\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 7) Train/test split\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"We split the dataset into training and test sets to estimate how well the model generalizes.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f1b50833\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"    X_encoded,\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"    y,\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"    test_size=0.2,\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"    random_state=42,\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"    stratify=y,\\n\",\n",
    "\t\")\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"784b3578\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 8) Train Gaussian Naive Bayes\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"Naive Bayes is a simple probabilistic classifier.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"8f4f08c9\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"from sklearn.naive_bayes import GaussianNB\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"model = GaussianNB()\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"model.fit(X_train, y_train)\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f1f1a90c\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## 9) Evaluate\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"We print:\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- **Accuracy** (overall correctness)\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- **Classification report** (precision/recall/F1)\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- **Confusion matrix** (error breakdown)\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b866a279\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"print('Accuracy:', accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred))\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0))\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"print('Confusion matrix:\\\\n', confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred))\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b34e2d2c\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "\t\"## Conclusion\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- If accuracy is low, consider: feature scaling (if needed), better encoding (for categorical data), or trying a different Naive Bayes variant.\\n\",\n",
    "\t\"- Always verify that the preprocessing applied to training data is **also** applied to new/unseen data.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9c5a7034\"\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
